      "narration": "David also has pretax retirement funds in a former employer's four-oh-one-k plan. He considers an eligible direct rollover into a traditional individual retirement account. Direct payment goes to the eligible receiving arrangement and avoids mandatory twenty percent withholding. Moving eligible pretax funds into a Roth arrangement instead generally introduces conversion income. If an annuity is used inside the traditional account, the account already provides tax deferral. The annuity must be evaluated for its other actual features, charges and restrictions. Do not describe an additional layer of tax deferral as an automatic benefit of placing an annuity inside an already tax-deferred retirement account.",
