      "title": "Read what continues when the annuitant dies",
      "narration": "Compare two fictional income quotes with identical starting funds and no other features. Pure life pays nine hundred dollars monthly while Rosa lives and stops at her death. A life option with a ten-year certain period pays eight hundred fifty dollars monthly, continuing for her life and guaranteeing the stated minimum payment period. If she dies after exactly twenty-four monthly payments under the second option, ninety-six guaranteed monthly payments remain for the beneficiary under these assumptions. If she lives beyond ten years, her lifetime payments continue. The certain period is a minimum guarantee, not the end of lifetime income. The quoted amounts are teaching assumptions; actual rates depend on the contract and its pricing.",
